 "about": "Source register (plan 2). Every outlet sits in one tier. original: the outlet did the reporting, or it is the organisation itself speaking about its own work (a lab's blog, a regulator, a club). secondary: good outlets that mostly rewrite or reprint others' reporting; fine as a source, but cite the original when it is open to read. lead: social posts, forums, press-release wires, aggregators and rumour mills. A lead-only outlet can point you to a story, but the checker refuses a story whose only source is lead only. An outlet not listed here passes and is shown as 'not yet rated'; add it to a tier when it turns up often. A web address matches its own domain and every sub-domain; the longest match wins.",
